meta {
  name: Start Import Master Data Job
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/master-data/branch/import-from-tenant/jobs
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

script:post-response {
  const data = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
  if (data && data.id) bru.setVar("importJobId", data.id);
}

docs {
  Starts the branch-admin **Import Master Data** (Tenant → Branch Master Data) as a
  background job and returns **202** with the job straight away — the dialog then
  polls `GET .../jobs/{{importJobId}}` once a second.

  Same sync as `POST /master-data/branch/import-from-tenant` (same matching,
  pre-flight, permissions), and still ONE atomic transaction: tests are reported in
  batches of 100, but nothing is saved until the whole import commits. A failure at
  any point rolls everything back.

  Response `data`: `{ id, branchId, status: "RUNNING", progress, result: null,
  error: null, startedAt, finishedAt, updatedAt }` — see "Get Import Master Data Job".

  **409 `MASTER_DATA_IMPORT_ALREADY_RUNNING`:** an import is already running for
  this tenant (imports run one at a time). Same branch → attach via
  "Get Active Import Master Data Job". **400** without an active branch in the JWT.
  Permissions: as the synchronous import.
}
